  "interpretation": "The patch refactors app/db.py to return plain Python dictionaries instead of Pydantic Note models, aiming to reduce serialization overhead. Validation passed, confirming API contract compliance. However, the runner rejected the change due to insufficient improvement. The candidate median latency (0.5177 ms) is slightly higher than the parent (0.5059 ms), resulting in a -1.33% relative improvement. While the mean latency increased marginally (0.5139 ms vs 0.5079 ms), the critical metric for this objective—median-of-repetition mean—did not decrease. The hypothesis that bypassing Pydantic validation would yield significant gains was not supported by the measured data. The noise levels (CV ~1%) suggest stable measurements, making the slight regression statistically observable. The change failed to meet the performance objective.",
  "limitations": [
    "Interpretation relies solely on aggregate latency metrics; per-operation breakdowns do not show improvement.",
    "No statistical significance testing or confidence intervals are provided for the latency difference.",
    "The candidate's median latency is higher than the parent, contradicting the optimization goal.",
    "Relative improvement is negative, indicating a regression rather than an enhancement."
